# The telemetry package's command, for a launch nobody configured by hand.
#
# Every launcher that starts a run tags it through `core/tools/run_telemetry.sh`, which runs the
# command named on the line below. The name is a bare command name, run from
# `~/.kensaiapp/venv/bin/` and nowhere else. A launch whose environment names no command takes
# this one. `core/tools/telemetry_command.py` reads this file as data, from the host whose core the
# launch runs on, so a launch from a pin and a launch for a satellite read it too.
#
# Without this line, every launcher's run goes uninstrumented.
#
# A launch whose environment sets the variable keeps its own value, and this line is not read for
# it. An empty value there still counts and reads as unconfigured, so setting the variable empty
# switches telemetry off for that one launch.
#
# An edit here reaches every later launch on this machine, a launch from a pin made earlier
# included.
KENSAIAPP_TELEMETRY_COMMAND=ka-telemetry
